# Live-diagnostics buffer snapshot: the IDE plugin writes an unsaved editor
# buffer to %TEMP%\drag-lint-live-<tickcount>.pas and lints THAT, so the file
# base name is a synthetic temp that never matches any real unit name. The
# unit-name-matches-file rule must SKIP such buffers (else it fires on every
# unsaved edit of every unit -- the SOFTWID.PAS live-lint false positive).
# Unit name "SoftWid" != file base "drag-lint-live-99999", yet must NOT fire.
!unit-name-matches-file
